==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la}} [[ballista]], a military siege engine for throwing stones

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{not comparable}} Or relating to [[ballistics]].
# {{comparable}} Or relating to [[projectile]]s moving under their own [[momentum]] and [[gravity]].
# {{comparable|US|slang}} Very [[angry]].
#: ''When he heard him lie about it, he '''went ballistic'''.''

